<Project>
  <!-- Same build settings the library had inside the CareCrew solution (2026-10-03). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Deterministic>false</Deterministic>
    <RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>False</RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- NuGet package metadata shared by Xaf.EditDraft.Core and Xaf.EditDraft.Blazor. Only those two projects set
       IsPackable=true; tests and the sample stay unpackable. The version is the single place to bump; the publish
       workflow (.github/workflows/publish-package.yml) runs on a tag v<Version>. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <Version>0.4.0-preview.1</Version>
    <Authors>Dave Bates</Authors>
    <Company>JapanDave95</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2026 Dave Bates</Copyright>
    <Product>Xaf.EditDraft</Product>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/JapanDave95/Xaf.EditDraft</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/JapanDave95/Xaf.EditDraft</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageTags>xaf;devexpress;blazor;xpo;draft;autosave;recovery</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.4.0-preview.1 (2026-10-05): BREAKING. Access to drafts is XAF security plus one optional host check; the library no longer knows a host's scope or owner kind (docs/xaf-native-access-2026-10-05.md; upgrade steps: docs/consumer-guide.md, "Upgrading from 0.3.0-preview.1"). Removed: EditDraftTypePolicy.ScopeOf and OwnerKind; EditDraftOwnerKind; EditDraftOwnerRule; EditDraftStoreBase.ScopeOid and OwnerFlag (the library no longer reads or writes their columns; a host that keeps the columns declares them on its own store class); EditDraftSeed.ScopeOid and OwnerFlag; EditDraftOwnerInfo.OwnerFlag; EditDraftRecreateDraft.ScopeOid; IEditDraftRecordAccess, XafSecurityEditDraftRecordAccess and EditDraftServices.RecordAccess; IEditDraftRecreateHost.IsScopeVisible; IEditDraftRecreateCandidate.IsVisible; EditDraftRecreateOutcome.SubSectionNotVisible and FilledNotVisible; EditDraftTextSet.RecreateSubSectionNotVisible. New: IEditDraftAccessCheck (MayRestore, MayRecreate), asked in addition to the library's XAF check, so a host can only narrow access; XafSecurityEditDraftAccessCheck (a saved record: loaded again through the application's secured object space and Write granted on it; a record rebuilt from a new-record draft: Create, Write and Read granted on it with its own values, uncommitted, as XAF checks a new object before it saves it; no request security: allowed, as XAF allows); EditDraftServices.AccessCheck, MayRestore and MayRecreate; EditDraftRecreateOutcome.FilledNotPermitted. Changed: IEditDraftOwnerResolver.Current takes the policy of the draft's type (null when the type is not registered); EditDraftRecreate.Run and IEditDraftRecreateHost.CurrentOwner take the type; the drafts list reads each owner the owner seam names per type and lists a row only under its type's owner; EditDraftTypePolicy.IsGeneric is "has a decision table"; a new-record row whose type the login may not create stays in the list with Open disabled; the offer asks the access check once there is a draft to offer; RecordNotVisible reads "no permission" in both text sets; log lines name no host rule. Earlier: 0.3.0-preview.2 (2026-10-05): same content as the unpublished 0.3.0-preview.1 (its release run stopped at a test that pinned the previous version number; that test now follows the version instead). 0.3.0-preview.1: adds the client-side input journal, OFF by default (docs/edit-draft-client-journal-design-2026-10-03.md and the M1/M1b write-ups). New: an ES module served as a static web asset (_content/Xaf.EditDraft.Blazor/edit-draft-journal.js) that keeps what the user is typing in a focused editor in localStorage, one key per entry and per page load, so it survives a refresh, a lost connection or a crash; EditDraftJournalAttributeControllerBlazor puts a server-built data-editdraft descriptor on each captured DetailView editor; switch key EditDraftCapture:Journal:Enabled (fail closed, together with the type key); EditDraftTypePolicy.JournalTimeOfDayMembers; EditDraftTexts.JournalRowLabel (ja/en); Core rules for entries, budgets (60 entries, 12,000 characters, 60 minutes per page load), format- and culture-bound conversion. Clears act on the page load's own entries only; another page load's entries are removed only when its Web Lock is gone; a logoff sweep removes the namespace. Not yet included: the server intake that turns journal entries into restorable drafts (M3) and masked-editor reply matching (M2), so enabling the key journals but does not restore. Earlier: 0.2.0-preview.1 (2026-10-04): closes the 15 library gaps found by the sample consumer (docs/close-gaps-2026-10-04.md). New: startup checks that stop the application with a message naming the fix (store registered, a policy while capture is on, SQL Server, the store table named the same by XPO and the library, non-persistent object space provider), remembered per store class and database only after they pass; an optional table check that warns at setup and stops the XAF database update when the table is still missing after the schema update; EditDraftSecurity.DenyStoreToAllRoles for the ModuleUpdater and a best-effort startup warning for each role that may read the store; opt-in retention sweep (EditDraftRetention.Sweep, services.AddEditDraftRetention(), key EditDraftCapture:Retention:Enabled, application clock, interval at most 1440 minutes, 0 or below turns the hosted sweep off); the store table's schema and name come only from the store class's XPO mapping ([Persistent("schema.table")], default dbo), with quoted identifiers; EditDraftDecisions helpers; EditDraftBlazorOptions.HeaderActionOnEveryView; docs/consumer-guide.md. Changed: public renames LoginIsStaffMember to OwnerFlag, SubSectionOid to ScopeOid (store, seed, recreate draft), SubSectionOf to ScopeOf, IsSubSectionVisible to IsScopeVisible, EditDraftOwnerKind.F2StaffMember to HostDefined, EditDraftCaptureControllerBlazor to EditDraftCaptureController (store columns unchanged, no migration); English texts without host terms and without the promise of deletion at expiry; the header action shows caption and image; the row icon no longer re-enables an icon XAF disabled (O-11); an absent store table is re-checked after 30 seconds; Core grants InternalsVisibleTo only to Xaf.EditDraft.Blazor and Xaf.EditDraft.Tests. Unchanged: SQL Server only, XPO, Guid keys, DevExpress 26.1.4 as the tested floor, the Japanese text set.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- The repository README is the package README for both packages. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
